{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01TYjr7s8EW8jZDo6JqXJijy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright 2025 MIT Lincoln Laboratory\n2\t// Permission is hereby granted, free of charge,\n3\t// to any person obtaining a copy of this software\n4\t// and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"),\n5\t// to deal in the Software without restriction,\n6\t// including without limitation the rights to use, copy,\n7\t// modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense,\n8\t// and/or sell copies of the Software,\n9\t// and to permit persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so,\n10\t// subject to the following conditions:\n11\t//\n12\t// The above copyright notice and this permission notice\n13\t// shall be included in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n14\t//\n15\t// THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND,\n16\t// EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO\n17\t// THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n18\t// FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT.\n19\t// IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE\n20\t// FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT,\n21\t// TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE\n22\t// OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.\n23\t\n24\t//! C ABI surface of the translation.\n25\t//!\n26\t//! `c_src/src/main.c` compiled with `gcc -shared -fPIC` exports exactly two\n27\t//! dynamic symbols:\n28\t//!\n29\t//! ```text\n30\t//! T driver\n31\t//! T main\n32\t//! ```\n33\t//!\n34\t//! This module re-exports the translated implementations under those same\n35\t//! names so that the Rust `cdylib` is a drop-in, `dlopen`-able twin of the C\n36\t//! shared object.  It deliberately contains no logic of its own — every\n37\t//! behavioural decision lives in `src/main.rs`, which is shared verbatim\n38\t//! between the executable and this library.\n39\t\n40\t#![allow(dead_code)]\n41\t\n42\t#[path = \"main.rs\"]\n43\tmod prog;\n44\t\n45\t/// `void driver(int x)` — see `prog::driver`.\n46\t///\n47\t/// # Safety\n48\t/// Plain C ABI function; writes the formatted result to `stdout`.\n49\t#[no_mangle]\n50\tpub extern \"C\" fn driver(x: core::ffi::c_int) {\n51\t    prog::driver(x as i32);\n52\t}\n53\t\n54\t/// `int main(void)` — see `prog::run`.\n55\t///\n56\t/// Reads one integer from `stdin` with `scanf(\"%d\", &x)` semantics, calls\n57\t/// `driver`, and returns `0` exactly like the C `main`.\n58\t///\n59\t/// Note that this calls [`prog::run`] rather than `prog::main`: the C `main`\n60\t/// compiled into a shared object does not modify signal dispositions, so the\n61\t/// `SIGPIPE` restoration that the *executable* entry point performs must not\n62\t/// happen here.\n63\t///\n64\t/// # Safety\n65\t/// Plain C ABI function; consumes from `stdin` and writes to `stdout`.\n66\t///\n67\t/// `cfg(not(test))` only because `cargo test --lib` compiles this crate into a\n68\t/// test harness that generates its own `main`; the `cdylib` artifact is never\n69\t/// built with `--test`, so the export is always present in the real `.so`.\n70\t#[cfg(not(test))]\n71\t#[no_mangle]\n72\tpub extern \"C\" fn main() -> core::ffi::c_int {\n73\t    prog::run();\n74\t    0\n75\t}\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_016tYVJgjag8saeJ3LxydRMU","session_id":"48be53e8-e7f1-4c70-a7a7-6c40e01deca5","uuid":"667e8fd5-fbea-4e19-9850-c92574424d36","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:04:51.723Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Adversarial C-vs-Rust review"}
