\"memory allocation of 4096 bytes failed\\nnote: run with `RUST_BACKTRACE=1` ...\"\n        SIGABRT (status 134)                 (consumed 0 bytes)\n```\nReproducible window on this host: `RLIMIT_AS` ≈ 3,140,000 – 3,266,000 bytes (8/8 runs identical). Below ~3.1 MB both fail in `ld.so`; above ~3.27 MB both work.\n\n### D4 — `setvbuf` on stdin (coreutils `stdbuf`, any LD_PRELOAD) affects C only (executable, environment)\nBecause the translation reimplements the buffering instead of using glibc's `FILE`, `stdbuf` is a no-op for it, so the consumed-byte count diverges on non-seekable stdin:\n```\n$ python3 -c \"import sys;sys.stdout.buffer.write(b'42 '+b'z'*997)\" | { stdbuf -i0 <driver>; printf LEFT=; wc -c; }\n  C   : 384  LEFT=997      (1-byte reads)\n  Rust: 384  LEFT=0\n$ ... stdbuf -i512 ...\n  C   : 384  LEFT=488\n  Rust: 384  LEFT=0\n```\n(Seekable stdin matches, because the exit-time `lseek` lands on the same byte either way.)\n\n### D5 — stdout flush happens too early relative to exit-time code\nC's `printf` output sits in glibc's fully-buffered stdout `FILE` until `_IO_cleanup`, i.e. *after* all destructors/atexit handlers; `driver()` flushes immediately. With `LD_PRELOAD=pre.so` (ctor + dtor + atexit writing to fd 1):\n```\n  C   : [CTOR][DTOR][ATEXIT]384\\n\n  Rust: [CTOR]384\\n[DTOR][ATEXIT]\n```\nSame for stdout=file and stdout=pipe.\n\n### D6 — cdylib `main` is not stateful: repeated calls lose the buffered leftovers (shared object)\n`prog::run()` builds a fresh `CStdin` per call and drops the read-ahead; glibc keeps it in the persistent `stdin` FILE. With `loader2 <so> N` and stdin = pipe `\"42 99 7\"`:\n```\n  N=2  C: 384\\n498\\n      Rust: 384\\n300\\n\n  N=3  C: 384\\n498\\n314\\n Rust: 384\\n300\\n300\\n\n```\nSeekable stdin matches (the `lseek`-back rescues it); pipes/fifos/sockets/ttys do not.\n\n### D7 — cdylib exports bypass the host process's glibc stdio (shared object)\nSame root cause as D5/D6, but visible without any preload (`loader3`, `loader4`):\n```\nhost printf(\"A\"); main(); printf(\"B\")   C: A384\\nB          Rust: 384\\nAB\nhost getchar(); main()                  C: [got 52]304\\n     Rust: 300\\n[got 52]\n                                        (final file offset 2)        (offset 1)\ndriver(1); write(1,\"|X|\"); driver(2)    C: |X|302\\n304\\n     Rust: 302\\n|X|304\\n\n```\n\n## (b) Tested and matching (no divergence)\n\n- **Inputs**: ~6,000 seekable-stdin cases + 2,780 numeric/byte-soup cases + 2,350 boundary cases + 49 pipe cases (up to 5 MB). Covered signs, lone signs, `- 5`, leading zeros (up to 4096), `0x`/`0X`/`0b`, `,`/`.`/`e`, NUL and ≥0x80 bytes, all six C-locale whitespace bytes, no-trailing-newline, LONG/INT boundaries ±1, 5 MB digit runs, 5 MB whitespace runs, random 0–255 soup.\n- **Buffer-boundary / `st_blksize` rule**: every token type (`0`, `0x`, `-`, `-5`, `5x`, `\\0`, 19-digit, …) placed at offsets 4086–4106 and 8182–8202, with and without trailing junk — the `blksize>0 && blksize<BUFSIZ` rule and the single-`ungetc` accounting are correct in all branches (whitespace-only+EOF, sign+EOF, sign+non-digit, digit+EOF, digit+non-digit, leading-`0` probe). Also verified against `blksize=1024` (`/proc/*`, ttys), not just 4096.\n- **stdin types**: regular file (offset 0/mid/EOF), `O_APPEND`, `O_RDWR`, empty, directory, closed, write-only, `O_PATH`, fifo, unix socketpair (STREAM/DGRAM/SEQPACKET), `O_NONBLOCK` (empty and partial data), `/dev/zero`, `/dev/null`, `/dev/full`, `memfd`, `O_DIRECT`, `eventfd`, `/proc/{version,self/cmdline,self/stat}`, pty in canonical mode (line-at-a-time reads, 900/1023/1024/1025/2000/3000-byte lines, `\\x04` EOF, two lines) and raw mode.\n- **stdout**: pipe, regular file, `/dev/full` (ENOSPC), closed fd 1, closed fd 2, stdout == stdin fd (`O_RDWR`), tty, datagram/seqpacket sockets. **Both emit exactly one 4-byte `write` of `\"384\\n\"`** — proven by datagram message framing and by identical `RLIMIT_FSIZE` partial-write/SIGXFSZ behaviour (limits 0–10: identical bytes on the file, identical signal 25).\n- **Timing/signals**: `SIGSTOP`+`SIGCONT` during a blocking read, byte-at-a-time chunked pipe writes across the 4096 boundary, blocked (not ignored) SIGPIPE.\n- **Locale**: the C source never calls `setlocale`, so it always runs in the `\"C\"` locale; `is_c_space`/`is_ascii_digit` match glibc's C-locale tables exactly — no locale env var can diverge.\n- **Non-finding**: at `RLIMIT_NOFILE = 4` both fail to exec (exit 127) but `ld.so`'s stderr text differs (`libc.so.6` vs `libgcc_s.so.1`), since the Rust binary needs one more shared object. No limit exists where one runs and the other does not.\n\nExperiment scripts and helpers are all under `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-pTQYiQ/tmp/audit/` (`runner.c`, `sigpipe.c`, `sigpipe2.c`, `nofile.c`, `rlim.c`, `rlim2.c`, `rlimpipe.c`, `loader2-4.c`, `pre.c`, `fuzz.py`, `fuzz2.py`, `fuzz3.py`, `t_pipe.py`, `t_fds.py`, `t_closed.py`, `t_pty2.py`, `t_dgram.py`, `t_exotic.py`, `t_timing.py`, `t_so.py`, `t_so2.py`, `t_stdbuf_pipe.sh`, `pydemo.py`). No repository file was modified."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":1771929,"totalTokens":158683,"totalToolUseCount":43,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1396,"cache_read_input_tokens":150618,"output_tokens":6667,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2941},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1396},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":4,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":39,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
