{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_sgjfnoe7b6wpin7hum2etnza6hthwfyjyyxrr3qfamh7oilhgxza","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass, and the work found and fixed **four real divergences**.\n\n## What the project actually is\n\n`c_src/` contains a single 12-line translation unit built by CMake as an **executable** (`add_executable`), not a library. `Cargo.toml` declares **no `[features]`** and `CMakeLists.txt` has no options/`#ifdef`s, so there is exactly **one valid build configuration** (`--no-default-features` ≡ default). To still do real FFI-level differential testing I compiled the C as a `.so` (`gcc -fPIC -shared`) and added a `cdylib` target (`src/ffi.rs`) that re-exports the same two symbols — so tests load **both** `.so`s with `libloading` and never call Rust directly.\n\n## Phase A artifacts\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C `.so` exports exactly `driver` + `main`; the Rust `.so` exports the same two. `nm -D` diff is **empty**; `ldd -r` shows 0 undefined symbols.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 24 rows. The C has *zero* explicit error checks, so the surface is `scanf`'s failure modes (input failure, matching failure, `ERANGE` clamp), the `printf` failure modes, and the FFI/process boundaries.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 30 rows, all `[x]`, covering the `driver` symbol, the `.so`'s `main` via an external C loader, and the executable pipeline.\n\n## Divergences found and fixed (C was always right)\n1. **`SIGPIPE` killed the C, not the Rust** — Rust's runtime installs `SIG_IGN`; C dies with signal 13 (rc 141) on a closed-pipe `stdout`.\n2. **…and the reverse** — naively forcing `SIG_DFL` broke the case where `SIG_IGN` was *inherited* across `execve` (C survives, Rust died). Fixed by capturing the inherited disposition in an ELF `.init_array` constructor (runs *before* Rust's rt init) and reinstalling it.\n3. **`stdin` consumption** — Rust's `io::Stdin` swallowed 8192 bytes and never gave them back; glibc reads `st_blksize`, `ungetc`s the terminator, and `lseek`s a seekable fd back at exit. `{ ./driver; ./driver; ./driver; } < \"42 99 7\"` printed `384 300 300` instead of C's `384 498 314`. Fixed with a `CStdin` reader.\n4. **Allocation failure aborted** — under `ulimit -v 3125` C printed `384` while Rust died with `SIGABRT` + stderr. Fixed by making the program allocation-free (inline `[u8; BUFSIZ]`, stack-formatted single-`write` output — still exactly one 4-byte `write`, verified via datagram framing).\n\n## Results\n`./verify.sh` → **ALL PHASES PASSED**: 75 differential tests (24 + 28 + 8 + 8 + 7) across thousands of randomized fixed-seed inputs, plus 11 500 ad-hoc fuzz cases comparing stdout, stderr, exit code, terminating signal, and shared-fd leftovers — 0 divergences.\n\n`ERRORS.md` also documents 6 **residual** differences I deliberately did not fake (R1–R6: `stdbuf`/`LD_PRELOAD` reaching into glibc's `FILE`, repeated `dlsym`'d `main` calls on a pipe, `RLIMIT_AS` below the Rust binary's load footprint). Each requires a third party inside the same process or an artificial memory limit; none is reachable through the program's own input, output, or exit status. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified (source hashes recorded; only the prescribed `c_src/build/` was added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":943,"cache_read_input_tokens":252991,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":943,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48be53e8-e7f1-4c70-a7a7-6c40e01deca5","uuid":"b92a1842-3f33-489b-8376-e3a744209b2f","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:43:17.653Z"}
